      <section id="tb5-bandwidth" class="tb5-bandwidth" hidden aria-label="Thunderbolt 5 bandwidth modes">
        <h2>Same four lanes. Two bandwidth modes.</h2>
        <div class="bandwidth-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Illustrate a bandwidth mode"><button type="button" data-bandwidth="normal" aria-pressed="true">Normal · 80/80</button><button type="button" data-bandwidth="boost" aria-pressed="false">Bandwidth Boost · 120/40</button></div>
        <div aria-live="polite"><div class="bandwidth-flow"><strong id="bandwidth-out">80 Gbps →</strong><strong id="bandwidth-back">← 80 Gbps</strong></div><p id="bandwidth-lanes">2 lanes each way</p><p id="bandwidth-explanation">Normal operation provides 80 Gbps in each direction at the same time.</p></div>
        <p class="model-note">This control illustrates lane allocation. Connected hardware negotiates the real mode. Each lane uses one differential pair; the 3D wiring stays the same.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="part-panel" aria-label="Cable components">
      <div id="component-explanation" class="part-description" aria-live="polite"><a class="back-to-model" href="#model-stage">Back to model ↑</a><h2 id="part-name">Explore a component</h2><p id="part-summary">Select a part of the cable or choose a component from the list to learn how it works.</p><details id="part-details" hidden><summary>Technical detail &amp; sources</summary><p id="part-detail">{{ explorer.parts[0].detail }}</p><p id="part-whatcable-detail">{{ explorer.parts[0].whatcableDetail }}</p><a id="part-source" href="#reference-sources">Reference specification</a></details><div id="part-whatcable" class="whatcable-context" hidden><h3>How WhatCable helps</h3><p id="part-whatcable-text"></p></div></div>
